  "id": "BIT-seaweedfs-2026-129852",
  "summary": "SeaweedFS before 4.42 File Existence Disclosure via VolumeServer.FetchAndWriteNeedle",
  "details": "SeaweedFS before 4.42 contains an information disclosure vulnerability that allows unauthenticated attackers to probe local files by supplying a filesystem path in gcs_google_application_credentials. Attackers can send crafted gRPC FetchAndWriteNeedle requests and use differing error messages to learn file existence, readability, and partial content shape on the host.",
